1
00:00:01,220 --> 00:00:07,541
If you dropped Mount Everest into the deepest part of the ocean, it would disappear.

2
00:00:07,611 --> 00:00:11,293
This is the Mariana Trench, in the western Pacific.

3
00:00:11,363 --> 00:00:17,825
Everest stands eight thousand eight hundred and forty-nine metres tall.

4
00:00:17,895 --> 00:00:24,485
The bottom of the trench, the Challenger Deep, is almost eleven thousand metres down.

5
00:00:24,557 --> 00:00:28,744
So its summit would still sit more than two kilometres under water.

6
00:00:28,994 --> 00:00:33,434
The trench is over two and a half thousand kilometres long.

7
00:00:33,628 --> 00:00:36,111
Roughly London to Moscow.

8
00:00:36,181 --> 00:00:41,718
At the bottom, eight tons press on every square inch.

9
00:00:41,788 --> 00:00:44,148
And yet, things live down there.

10
00:00:44,282 --> 00:00:47,709
Tiny shrimp-like animals called amphipods.

11
00:00:47,779 --> 00:00:51,313
Humans first reached the bottom in 1960.

12
00:00:51,363 --> 00:00:53,597
Just two men.

13
00:00:54,047 --> 00:01:00,018
Even today, far more people have been to space than to the bottom of this trench.
